ivery-integrity-register.rkt (commit c84d43eef90f)' - the wave's first source-trio commit had bundled the register fixture's 150-column reflow. The refusal exposed a real defect in this wave's own tool: register F4's letter protects the FINAL record commit ('the final record commit must be evidence-only', echoed by prepare()'s own contract comment 'inspects the newest base..head commit touching the evidence directory'), but the tool scanned every historical commit, so a delivery whose newest record commit is pure was refused - the F1 defect class (declaration vs behavior) in the wave's own guard, caught by the wave's own ladder. Repaired in #9736 (merged 29a4e62b: the newest evidence-touching commit is inspected; mixed-final still refused with precise foreign paths; a third test direction pins older-impure + newer-pure -> pure), after which prepare accepted the delivery and staged this binding trio. The mixed commit c84d43eef90f itself remains in the delivered history, named here and in the wave report section 8 rather than hidden."))) (remaining-items . (#hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W4 owner (delivery-tool API contract)") (rationale . "The gate's --receipt-head cross-check is exercised by tests, the raw captures and this binding's gate, but production head binding is enforced by the coordinator's expected-head path and gsd-delivery.py review()/require_receipt_tip; wiring a production caller to pass the durable receipt head to the gate belongs with the delivery-tool API contract work.")) #hasheq((classification . "deferred-noncritical") (owner . "W5 owner (artifact provenance and determinism)") (rationale . "The gate receives the content digest as a caller-supplied --content-digest value and only checks that the record agrees with what it was handed, so the chain 'recompute the digest from the diff' lives outside the gate that enforces it - the F1 shape one level up. The wave ships the tool that computes the digest and binds its own re